From 331d6cc83600cd036bdba02defd7d8556687ec08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:01:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P0: least-privilege ChatGPT OAuth scopes and read-only Gemini
 OAuth lane

- Fix silent scope escalation: authorize() no longer force-adds
  execute_approved/write_noncanonical. Default scopes are read + propose;
  elevated scopes are advertised and grantable only when listed in
  CFP_CHATGPT_OAUTH_ELEVATED_SCOPES. Restores the 2 failing contract tests
  without changing them.
- Provider lane configuration (state prefix, subject, consent URL, resource,
  scopes) so additional lanes reuse ChatGPTOAuthProvider. Empty prefix keeps
  existing ChatGPT oauth_state rows valid.
- Gemini lane /mcp-gemini (AI 691141): read scope only, DCR disabled,
  pre-registered client seeded from CFP_GEMINI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID/SECRET,
  exact redirect URI match, dedicated consent admin token, state isolated
  under the gemini: prefix so tokens are not accepted across lanes.
- Tests: Gemini contract (9 cases) in an isolated process.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tau1ZNKJRKPvMHsB5GHyYQ
